  <section>
    <h2>Correlation Function</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Definition</h3>
        <pre><code>ξ(r): excess probability of finding galaxy pair
ξ(r) = (r/r₀)^(-γ) (power law)
r₀: correlation length (~ 5 Mpc for SDSS)
γ: slope (~ 1.8)</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Power Spectrum</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Definition</h3>
        <pre><code>P(k): Fourier transform of ξ(r)
Galaxy bias: b = δ_galaxy/δ_matter
P_galaxy(k) = b² × P_matter(k)
Redshift space distortions: fσ₈</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>BAO</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Properties</h3>
        <pre><code>Sound horizon: ~ 150 Mpc
Standard ruler: fixed physical scale
Imprints on galaxy clustering
Measures expansion history
Complementary to CMB</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

